; Zone file of the server in the e2e rig, origin local-ip.test.
; The default TTL is stated so that the TTL written on one record does not become the default of the records after it.
$TTL 300
; This delegation exists only so the e2e suite can verify referrals.
; 192.0.2.53 is a documentation address (RFC 5737) where nothing answers.
e2e-delegated      NS  ns1.e2e-delegated
ns1.e2e-delegated  A   192.0.2.53
; Records that exist only so the e2e suite can verify each supported type; e2e-alias has a TTL of its own so that the suite sees a declared TTL served.
e2e-records       A      192.0.2.10
e2e-records       AAAA   2001:db8::10
e2e-records       TXT    "local-ip.sh e2e" "second string"
e2e-records       MX     10 mail.example.net.
e2e-records       CAA    0 issue ";"
e2e-alias    600  CNAME  target.example.net.
_e2e._tcp         SRV    0 0 443 target.example.net.
@                 TXT    "local-ip.sh test instance"
; Two TXT sets that exist only so the e2e suite can verify truncation, EDNS and TCP: every reply for e2e-txt-udp is larger than 512 octets and smaller than 1232, and every reply for e2e-txt-tcp is larger than 1232. Each string is 180 octets and starts with its position so that no two records are equal.
e2e-txt-udp  TXT  "e2e-txt-udp record 1 of 4 xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
e2e-txt-udp  TXT  "e2e-txt-udp record 2 of 4 xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
